## Analyst Assessment

The simulated attack demonstrated that Sysmon and Wazuh successfully correlated multiple stages of malicious PowerShell activity.

The SIEM generated alerts throughout the attack chain, providing sufficient visibility for investigation and response.

No actual compromise occurred because this activity was executed within a controlled laboratory environment.

---

## Lessons Learned

- Sysmon significantly improves endpoint visibility.
- Wazuh successfully detected multiple PowerShell attack behaviors.
- Correlating multiple alerts provides better context than investigating isolated events.
- MITRE ATT&CK mapping improves incident classification and reporting.
